# REGRESSION — the TEMPORAL cell with a LIVE MECHANISM.
#
# Sibling of `cow_alias_severed_by_root_reassign_then_view.gg`, which pins the
# same ordering but cannot exercise anything: there the alias's buffer is
# never touched after the view, so no provenance decision is load-bearing.
# Here it IS. After the sever the view is taken, and then the ALIAS's own
# buffer is grown past a reallocation:
#
#     Vector[String] alias = v            # alias aliases v's storage
#     v = []                              # reassign: severs; alias takes its copy
#     String s = alias.get(0).unwrap()    # view into the buffer ALIAS now owns
#     ... grow ALIAS 64x -> realloc ...
#     print(s)                            # must survive
#
# WHAT IT PINS: that a view taken AFTER a sever is attributed to the collection
# the name refers to AFTER the sever. Root resolution walks the `Alias` chain,
# so the question is live: `alias` was `Alias(v)` before the reassignment, and
# resolving to that stale root would key the rescue on `v` -- which nothing
# mutates on a forward path from the bind -- leaving `s` dangling when `alias`
# reallocs. The correct attribution is `alias` itself.
#
# MECHANISM PIN: the sibling harness assertion checks the emitted GIR carries
# the lazy rescue (`__cow_mat`) for this program. stdout alone cannot
# distinguish "the rescue ran" from "nothing needed rescuing", and this is the
# one temporal cell where the rescue genuinely has to run -- its sibling emits
# no rescue at all.
#
# ⚠ Green on the pre-fix compiler too, like its sibling: the pre-fix
# provenance recorded the SPELLING `alias`, which post-sever happens to be the
# right answer. It is the fire count, not the rc, that makes this a pin.
#
# The lengths pin the sever direction: `alias` grew to 65 while `v` kept the
# single element it was given after the reassignment.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(mk("hel", "lo"))
    Vector[String] alias = v
    v = []
    v.push(mk("new", "one"))
    String s = alias.get(0).unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        alias.push(mk("fill", "er"))
        i = i + 1
    print(s)
    print(alias.len())
    print(v.len())
